  "query_preview": "..\n\nInbound high pressure expands into the central Great Lakes this \nevening/tonight and brings quiet weather conditions into tonight \nwith just a some high clouds streaming across the area tonight under\na light to calm wind. The high clouds will be focused across lower \nportions of southeast Michigan tonight. This will cause a difference \nin radiational cooling conditions with the Thumb and Saginaw Valley \nlikely being around the freezing mark tonight under more favorable \nconditions compared to locations towards the southern MI border that \nwill be about 10 degrees warmer for the overnight low. \n\nHigh pressure maintains influence over the region tomorrow as mostly \ndry conditions largely prevail. A warm front is forecast to lift \ntowards the region tied to a weakening shortwave lifting out of the \nsouthern Plains. Better theta-e surge and moisture transport will be \nto the west of Lake Michigan. Outgoing forecast remains dry Saturday \nand Saturday night, but a few isolated light showers may be possible \nwith the weak theta-e advection west of the forecast area that could \nencroach on western portions of southeast Michigan. Minimal QPF \nexpected if it does occur. \n\nHigh pressure lingers over the Atlantic coast early next week as \nwestern CONUS troughing marches into the plains during the mid week \nperiod. This will lead to a southerly wind component prevailing \nacross Michigan and bringing mild temperatures. Decent spread in long\nrange models in regards to timing of the next chance of \nprecipitation as longer wave troughing develops over the central \nplains with the potential for a secondary Canadian shortwave merging \nwith the broader trough. Broad brush of PoPs Monday night into \nWednesday highlight the uncertainty in timing. Forecast within this \npattern has daily highs in the 60s with increasing humidity helping \nkeep overnight lows in the 50s. Late week stands best chance for \ncold frontal passage bringing temperatures back to around the average\nfor this time of year.",
